{title: In the Hill Country}
{subtitle: Judges 10:1; 10:2}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] [Bb/D] | [Ab/C] [Bb7] | [Eb] [Bb/D] | [Ab/C] [Bb7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb7]After [Eb]Abimelech's [Bb/D]time was done [Ab/C]
[Ab]Tola son of [Eb/G]Puah rose up [Eb]
[Cm7]Son of Do[Bb/D]do in the [Cm7]sun
A [Ab]man of Issachar he [Bbsus4]was [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]He lived in [Bb/D]Shamir it is [Cm7]true [Eb/Bb]
[Ab]In the hill [Eb/G]country of Ep[Eb]hraim
[Cm7]He brought the peace [Bb/D]back to the [Cm7]view
And [Ab]saved the people from their [Bbsus4]whim
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He [Ab]judged Is[Bb]rael for [Eb]twen-ty-three
Years [Ab]of quiet [Bb]and stabil[Cm]ity
He served the [Ab]land with [Bb]gentle [Cm7]care
A judge who [Ab]lived with[Bb]out a [Eb]scare [Bb/D][Cm][Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]His lineage [Bb/D]from Dodo [Cm7]came [Bb6]
[Ab]From the tribe [Bb]that knew his [Eb]name
[Cm7]He exercised [Bb/D]his office [Cm7]well
[Bb6]In [Ab]the hill where the shadows [Bbsus4]fell
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He judged [Ab]Israel [Bb]for twen-ty-[Eb]three
Years [Ab]of quiet [Bb]and stabil[Cm]ity
He served the [Ab]land with [Bb]gentle [Cm]care
A judge who [Ab]lived with[Bb]out a [Eb]scare [Bb/D][Cm][Bb6]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ab]Then he died [Bb]and found his [Cm]rest [Bb6]
[Ab]Buried in [Bb]Shamir where he [Eb]blessed [Bb/D][Cm][Bb][Eb]
{end_of_verse}
